utils/fuzz-seam.py --seam-check (not an oracle): every --seam
variant of every program also checks each rule firing with the solver
(`premise => lhs = rhs`); no firing is invalid or unexpressible. Cells: the
Store-Map rules and the cross-object skips (A-INB firings); wide: ARM.
RUN: %python %sea_src_root/utils/fuzz-seam.py --sea-vc sea-vc %if !yices %{ --solver=z3 %} --seed 5 -n 2 --accesses=cells --seam-check | FileCheck %s
RUN: %python %sea_src_root/utils/fuzz-seam.py --sea-vc sea-vc %if !yices %{ --solver=z3 %} --seed 5 -n 3 --accesses=wide --seam-check | FileCheck %s
CHECK: seam-check-firings: {{[1-9][0-9]*}}
CHECK: seam-check-invalid: 0
CHECK: seam-check-unknown: 0
CHECK: seam-check-unexpressible: 0
CHECK: failures: 0

